  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Woof Haven Toulon is a 6,000 m² fully fenced forest dog park on Chemin Belle Visto. According to its website, it was born from the lack of suitable places for dogs in Toulon and the Var, the insecurity of hunting periods and the difficulty of offering freedom and safety to sensitive, runaway or reactive dogs. There is a pool, a ball pit, a fitness course, a scent board, a play and swimming area, and a picnic area with sea views. The park can be hired privately: a solution designed for sensitive, reactive or runaway dogs, or simply for a calm moment with your dog.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>Booking is online, once a complete file (vaccinations and insurance) has been sent. Prices shown for private hire: €10 for 30 minutes, €18 per hour and €35 for two hours, a booking lasting from 30 minutes to 2 hours, with the second private hire at half price. The park also offers one-hour dog recess sessions at €12 per dog, in groups of up to 9 dogs (sociable, vaccinated dogs), with games, exploring, an agility course and swimming, and activities led by a behaviourist trainer using positive methods: training, fitness course, mantrailing, truffle hunting (cavage).</p>
      <p>The rules: up-to-date CHPPiL vaccination (plus kennel cough and rabies for category 1 and 2 dogs), dog identified by microchip or tattoo, regular worming and parasite treatment, no sick or injured dog and no female in heat, adult customer. Dogs are never left alone and unsupervised, are not tied to fence posts, coercive methods and tools are prohibited and the equipment is reserved for dogs (not humans, children included). Smoking, lighting fires (including stoves or barbecues) and drinking alcohol are prohibited, as the park lies in a natural area at risk; pick up droppings. The rules advise against throwing balls or sticks when several dogs who do not know each other are present. Cancellations must be made at least 24 hours in advance; rain does not count as major bad weather.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: if your dog is fearful or reactive, book a private slot in advance and re-read the house rules on the park's website.</div>

      <h2>Worth checking before you go</h2>
      <p>The website is not consistent from one page to another: the home page announces private hire every day from 6am to 10pm and up to 8 dogs per session, whereas the general terms set slots (5:30pm-8pm on weekdays except Wednesday from 1:30pm, 8am-8pm at weekends) and 4 dogs at most unless an exception is made; the access code is announced 3 hours before the slot on one page and 30 minutes before on another. Check these points when you book.</p>
    </div>

